In other words, it's not in any sense of the word a 9GFLOP operation. It 
might get 9GOP, but a FLOP (especially a 64-bit FLOP, which is what Alpha 
hardware naturally does) is a lot  different than an OP.

Ebay isn't much of a reliable source of benchmarking information.

Admittedly, I have not seen any figures with AltiVec optimized BLAS, but 
everything I have seen indicates that an Alpha runs about twice as fast as 
a G4 if they're both at the same clock rate. And, multiprocessing on 
shared memory (like them Apple cube things do) does *not* give you double 
performance figures. At best, you'll get a couple of percentage points 
higher performance.

If anyone can do a direct comparison of some matrix-intensive BLAS code, 
I'd be real interested. The Apples have one advantage: they look cooler.

