J C S van de Sande writes:

> the first boot diskette with milo is installed after this I am
> unable to boot the generic.img It seems like it can't find the
> floppy disk.  I have tried <dev> e.g. sda1''[diskdrive fd0] but it
> don't do anything. How can I acces the floppy drive?

This should load "vmlinux" kernel from first floppy drive and then
prompt for ramdisk image to be loaded from another floppy in the same
drive:

  boot fd0:vmlinux root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1

Kernel needs to be on a filesystem that MILO supports, at least "fat"
and "ext2" should be supported by any MILO version.

One could also try to check the filesystem contents first:

  ls fd0:

If MILO loads from the floppy drive but cannot see the the floppy
drive itself, one might want to try another version of MILO.

