(sorry about the previous post)

> Are
> packages when they've been tested moved to Stable from Unstable on a
> rolling basis or are they only moved when a new version of Stable is ready
> for release.

Stable is the "released" versions and unstable is the versions included
in the next release. So, they're only moved on a per-release basis. You
can d/l stable packages and use: dpkg -i --force-downgrade <package>
or you could remove the unstable entries from /etc/apt/sources.list and 
do apt-get update then use dselect to uninstall/reinstall what you're
having problems with.  Also you can set a hold on packages so they
won't be upgraded unless you speicifically request it.

> I had been downloading direct from unstable but now my system takes quite
> a bit of time to shut down - about 10mins.

How/when does it stall?

James



