I bought an xp1000 el cheapo off of ebay.com and installed Debian on
it. I had a pc164sx which was running RH7.1. Basically I wanted the
most stable system I could get after having a few problems with my SX
so not knowing to much about Debian I installed Potato over ftp using
the broadband connection I've got at home. Potato was OK but there
didn't seem to be a fairly workable web browser. So after speaking to
the folks on the debian alpha list I upgraded to Woody which was a
significant improvement however I still had problems with Mozilla
bombing out on some web pages, so after further discussions I upgraded
to Mozila 1.0.3 which runs just fine. So now after a gradual install
process I'm running Debian Unstable with most of the uptodate packages
after about 2.5 months. I had some problems with a 2.4.18 kernel i
compiled from source in unstable so I've gone back to a 2.2 kernel and
everything runs just fine. It does everything my windows system does
but with two exceptions

1. there is no flash in the web browser - which quite frankly I
couldn't care much about.

2. There is no Java support in the browser, however which is something
I do need from time to time.

Thats why I'm writing this on my windows system.

Also another thing about debian is for want of a better expression it
doesn't come with cruise control like RH in other words you have to
fiddle around with it a bit more. For instance there is no sndconfig
like RH so you have to use modconf to select which modules you'd like
installed in the kernel ie pnp & the drivers for your sound
system/card.

I still use my debian system but i find I split my time between both,
I'm also going to get a hobbyist license of Open VMS but it's a bit
picky about hardware and my system came without a cdrom and hdd.

Just one peice of advice to people thinking of upgrading there
hardware - get broadband first. It's not so much the speed of your
system that's the problem it the network. My windows system is dual
PIII Xeon 550 -underclocked to 300mhz + 1mb cache each +196mb ram and
thats just fine. Those sort of cpu you can pick up for about $30 each
on ebay.com. It's running Windows 2000 server which I also pick up for
a fraction of it's price, on the net.

cheers,




