>ECC 100 Mhz memory (I heard that ECC memory you have to add in pairs,
>but not sure..)

You have to add _any_ memory in pairs for the 164LX board.  Memory
SIMMs are 32 bits wide (not counting parity) and the board has a
64-bit wide memory bus to match the 64-bit Alpha processor.

>Can I add 133MHz ECC Memory (it is $39 compared to $80 for 100Mhz
>at Fry's)

Anything faster than 83MHz should be OK.  And in fact for the 164LX
it doesn't even have to be so-called ECC (36 bits wide).

