Hi,

You need to use modconf to enable the modules for your sound card. A SB16
should work.


Also your etc/modules file should look something like this




# /etc/modules: kernel modules to load at boot time.
#
# This file should contain the names of kernel modules that are
# to be loaded at boot time, one per line.  Comments begin with
# a #, and everything on the line after them are ignored.
alias eth0 de4x5sb
sb
# alias sound sb
# pre-install sound insmod sound dmabuf=1
# alias midi opl3
# options opl3 io=0x388# /etc/modules: kernel modules to load at boot time.
#
# This file should contain the names of kernel modules that are
# to be loaded at boot time, one per line.  Comments begin with
# a #, and everything on the line after them are ignored.
alias eth0 de4x5sb
sb
# alias sound sb
# pre-install sound insmod sound dmabuf=1
# alias midi opl3
# options opl3 io=0x388
options sb io=0x220 irq=5 dma=1 
# ad1848
mpu401
options mpu401 io=0x330nfs
nfsd
options sb io=0x220 irq=5 dma=1 
# ad1848
mpu401
options mpu401 io=0x330nfs
nfsd



That's mine for sound on an xp1000

to find the irq/dma settings for your sound do a show device in srm or
show something i'm not sure type >>help in srm for more info.

Debian is a bit trickier than RH and other dists but it's worth it in the
end. Do a search for Alpha Debian + Sound on google for other tips.


http://www.linuxalpha.org/archives/axp-list/November2000/0238.shtml

